codex
The clean proof itself is discriminating: all seven submitted claims reconstructed as `#Top`, the manually embedded program term is constructor-identical to regenerated `solution.mpy`, a body mutation makes the universal theorem fail at the changed body, and the fresh false `"hello" → "ehllp"` postcondition builds but fails with the actual `"ehllo"` residual. I’m now checking whether the omitted CPython recursion exception is merely a partial-correctness boundary or a material “real program” mismatch.
